      "extract": "In 1995 Kashaev introduced a complex valued link invariant for an integer $N\\ge 2$ by using the quantum dilogarithm [@Kashaev:MODPLA95] and then he observed that his invariant grows exponentially with growth rate proportional to the volume of the knot complement for several hyperbolic knots [@Kashaev:LETMP97]. He also conjectured that this also holds for any hyperbolic knot, where a knot in the three-sphere is",
      "extractCut": true
